<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Paris (1898)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1898">1898</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war">Spanish–American War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Paris of December 1898 ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war">Spanish–American War</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> gave up <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>, which came under American military government, and ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a>, Guam and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, the last for 20 million dollars. It ended Spain's empire in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and made the United States a colonial power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1898.jpg" alt="Treaty of Paris (1898)" width="320" height="263" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frances Benjamin Johnston · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jules_Cambon_signs_Treaty_of_Paris,_1899.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
